From: SG Quality Lead R8 <danswett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:30:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] CI S2 combined: the workflow parts of 4b, 5a, 5b, 5c and 7a
 on the new main (Part of #4104)

One patch for Quality to apply on the S2 COMBINED branch ci/s2-combined3 at its head (see the pull request for the exact heads); the branch holds everything else.
Patch branch: sg-patch/ci-s2-combined-4104. Built on main 522bf1267849bce8ac11d2ba10c8af0ef9989604 (#4254 merged); apply only on an unmoved base.

What it does: ci.yml loses pwa-ui, pwa-e2e and the force-apt-fallback dispatch input (they run in FULL now); full.yml gains pwa-ui (six legs) and pwa-e2e, each checking out needs.trigger.outputs.tested and
using only the restore-only action; full-red.yml (new, 7a) opens one issue per red FULL job; pages.yml waits for FULL (5a).

Q10's notes: (a) the validator requires needs.trigger.outputs.tested and does not read head_repository; (b) the dispatched-sha on-main check is GONE (FULL has no dispatch sha; a run by hand tests the tip of
the ref it runs on); (c) the README cache bullet is fixed in the branch.

DECISION FOR QUALITY / R8c: the by-hand apt-fallback proof (quality/README.md section 4.7) had its input on ci.yml's workflow_dispatch; this patch removes it there (pwa-ui moves) and does NOT add it to
full.yml, because main's FullWorkflowTests (#4254) requires a run of FULL by hand to take no input at all. So that proof has no trigger now. Either keep it that way, or allow one boolean force-apt-fallback
input (no commit, never reaches a checkout) in that test; I did not decide it.

